# Supported GPUs:
This port is meant for the following cards that are no longer supported
by the current NVIDIA driver (590 and newer): Maxwell, Pascal and Volta.
For these, the 580 branch is the last one NVIDIA released, e.g.:

  Maxwell: GeForce GTX 750/750 Ti, GTX 900 series, Quadro M-series
  Pascal:  GeForce GTX 10 series, Quadro P-series
  Volta:   Titan V, Quadro GV100

For Turing (RTX 20 / GTX 16) and newer cards, use the official 'nvidia'
port. Kepler cards (GTX 600/700, Quadro K-series) need the 470 driver
branch and are not supported by this port.

# NOTE about groups and device permissions:
Add your user to the "video" group to be able to use the nvidia devices
required for 3D to function properly.

# NOTE about wayland and eglstream:
If wayland is installed and eglstream support is desired/needed,
additionally install the 'egl-wayland' port.

# NOTE about Settings:
Settings file that blacklists the nouveau kernel module and enables the
high-resolution console is installed (/etc/modprobe.d/nvidia-580xx.conf).

# Xorg NOUVEAU:
Remove xorg-xf86-video-nouveau if installed.

# Kernel version:
To build for a different kernel, set KVER, e.g.: KVER=6.18.56 pkgmk -d

# Credits:
Based on the 'nvidia' port from the CRUX opt collection, maintained
by Matt Housh (jaeger), as of commit 2cd81d7 in opt/ (the last version
on the 580 branch):

https://git.crux.nu/ports/opt/commit/2cd81d7198d102fd20a7e9412e7b85b003dbd096

# Changes from the original port:
- Builds only the proprietary (closed) kernel modules. NVIDIA's open
  modules don't support Maxwell, Pascal or Volta, so the
  NVIDIA_PROPRIETARY_MODULES variable is not needed and not used.
- The GSP firmware is not installed, since these cards don't use it.
- Installs /etc/modprobe.d/nvidia-580xx.conf.
- SYSSRC is set, so KVER builds for the kernel it names (taken from
  the newer CRUX port).
